# Editorial Architect UI

Canonical spec: `stitch_service_certify_prd/stitch_service_certify_prd/nexus_academy/DESIGN.md`. Tokens live in `src/routes/layout.css` (`@theme`). Tailwind v4 via `@tailwindcss/vite` — there is no `tailwind.config.js`.

## Tokens

- Primary: `#001b44` / container `#002f6c` (midnight)
- Action / success: secondary `#4a6700` and container `#bdf14f` — not generic “success green”
- Text: `on-surface` `#191c1d` — never pure black
- Type: Manrope (`font-headline`) + Inter (`font-body` / `font-label`)
- Utilities: `editorial-gradient`, `glass-card`, `shadow-ambient`

## The no-line rule

Do not use 1px solid borders to section content. Separate regions with surface shifts:

- Level 0: `bg-surface`
- Level 1: `bg-surface-container-low`
- Level 2 (cards): `bg-surface-container-lowest`

If a divider is required for a11y, use `outline-variant` at ~15% opacity.

## Components

- Primary CTA: `bg-secondary text-on-secondary` (e.g. Start practice)
- Cards: no divider lines; sit on a shifted surface
- Inputs: avoid boxed outlines; prefer `surface-container-high` fill
- Icons: `$lib/components/MaterialIcon.svelte` (wght font only; “filled” = weight 600)

## Do not

- Flat purple/indigo SaaS palettes, heavy drop shadows, or a second component library
- Import Google Fonts CSS when fontsource `wght.css` is already in `+layout.svelte`
- Import Material Symbols `full.css` (~3.8MB)
